  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a maintainer, I want every probe session built from an account session to keep that session's host policy, so that a test session restricted to the loopback host can never yield a request to the forum.\n\n### Scope\n\nFollow-up of #320 (PR #364, which adds `HFRSession.probe(cookies:now:)`, `package`, and uses it in `SessionRefreshFlow`). Three other flows build their probe with `HFRSession(cookies:)`, i.e. the `.forum` policy, whatever the source session's:\n\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/MPPoll/MPUnreadPoll.swift:26` (LOT-047): `makeProbe: { HFRSession(cookies: $0) }`.\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/Smileys/SmileyLookupFlow.swift:23` (LOT-053): the same default.\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/Login/LoginFlow.swift:18` (LOT-043): could build its fresh session with `session.probe(cookies: [], now:)` on its `into:` session.\n\nNo production impact (every production session is `.forum`): test hygiene, as #320.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Each default probe is built with `probe(cookies:now:)` on the source session (or the reason it cannot is stated).\n- [ ] An **offline** test per flow asserts the default probe's host policy (LESSONS 56: no test may rely on a local refusal that a mutation removes); each fails without the change.\n- [ ] `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; `scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes; the LOT-043, LOT-047 and LOT-053 specs updated (one line each).\n\nDepends on #364 being merged.\n",
